WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.521 --> 00:00:02.814
- [Narrator] In southern Pennsylvania,

00:00:02.814 --> 00:00:04.285
there is a battlefield.

00:00:04.285 --> 00:00:06.258
A battlefield so important
that it is thought

00:00:06.258 --> 00:00:09.495
to be the turning point
of the American Civil War.

00:00:09.495 --> 00:00:12.243
This is a story about that place.

00:00:12.243 --> 00:00:14.884
It's also a story about cats.

00:00:14.884 --> 00:00:18.134
Thousands and thousands of little cats.

00:00:23.017 --> 00:00:24.338
This is Rebecca.

00:00:24.338 --> 00:00:25.792
- Hi, I'm Rebecca.

00:00:25.792 --> 00:00:27.990
- [Narrator] And this is
her twin sister, Ruth.

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:30.279
- Hi, I'm Ruth and we run a museum

00:00:30.279 --> 00:00:34.446
of dioramas that are made
with handmade Civil War cats.

00:00:35.388 --> 00:00:38.134
- [Narrator] Civil War cats.

00:00:38.134 --> 00:00:40.244
The combination of a childhood love

00:00:40.244 --> 00:00:42.987
for clay cats and a strong fascination

00:00:42.987 --> 00:00:44.847
with the American Civil War.

00:00:44.847 --> 00:00:47.758
- [Rebecca] It started out
as a hobby that we just did

00:00:47.758 --> 00:00:50.886
as kids putzing around in our bedrooms.

00:00:50.886 --> 00:00:52.151
- [Narrator] That bit of child's play

00:00:52.151 --> 00:00:56.318
led to a full-fledged
museum which opened in 2013.

00:01:00.892 --> 00:01:03.017
- The two of us discussed
how much do we want

00:01:03.017 --> 00:01:04.579
to emphasize the cat thing.

00:01:04.579 --> 00:01:08.196
Because we don't want to come off as cutesy cats.

00:01:08.196 --> 00:01:10.500
The idea is the stories of the men,

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:12.172
not so much the fact that they're cats.

00:01:12.172 --> 00:01:15.166
They just are cats because they're cats.

00:01:15.166 --> 00:01:19.057
- [Narrator] Incredibly, each
of these scenes is to scale.

00:01:19.057 --> 00:01:21.974
- 1/8th of an inch equals
one foot in cat feet.

00:01:21.974 --> 00:01:24.502
Each one of our soldiers
represents one soldier

00:01:24.502 --> 00:01:25.844
who would've been on the field.

00:01:25.844 --> 00:01:26.918
We'll calculate the numbers

00:01:26.918 --> 00:01:28.237
that would have been left in the regiment

00:01:28.237 --> 00:01:31.306
and we'll fill it in with
that many cat soldiers.

00:01:31.306 --> 00:01:32.964
So for example, Little Round Top,

00:01:32.964 --> 00:01:35.963
we're going to eventually have
about 5,000 soldiers on it.

00:01:35.963 --> 00:01:37.421
Typically one like the Angle,

00:01:37.421 --> 00:01:39.793
we figure took us about
four-and-a-half years.

00:01:39.793 --> 00:01:42.581
The Little Round Top
diorama we figure is more

00:01:42.581 --> 00:01:45.165
of a five-or-six year diorama.

00:01:45.165 --> 00:01:46.734
- Oh look, ha!

00:01:46.734 --> 00:01:49.628
- We really just want
to make the Civil War

00:01:49.628 --> 00:01:52.007
more approachable, I guess, for people

00:01:52.007 --> 00:01:54.043
so they can relate to the history

00:01:54.043 --> 00:01:56.227
and have more of a connection

00:01:56.227 --> 00:01:58.802
with the men and the women involved.

00:01:58.802 --> 00:02:01.798
Now that the word of
this cat museum's out,

00:02:01.798 --> 00:02:03.731
all the people who love cats come in

00:02:03.731 --> 00:02:06.243
and now not only are
they seeing our dioramas,

00:02:06.243 --> 00:02:09.196
they're falling in love with the
five-and-a-half thousand furry smiles

00:02:09.196 --> 00:02:11.043
smiling at them.

00:02:11.043 --> 00:02:13.766
But, they're also learning the stories

00:02:13.766 --> 00:02:16.714
and suddenly they have an
appreciation of Gettysburg

00:02:16.714 --> 00:02:20.881
and the history, just because
they came to see the cats.

00:02:24.596 --> 00:02:26.929
(high note)

